From e8ca9651ea7d7d53c9568f3c1b4d9a992d821c3d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Thu, 18 Jun 2026 13:54:25 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02591/11362] [outer-loop] multi-paradigm model: add
 CLICK-INTERACTION paradigm tier -- unlocks su15/lp85/r11l (6/25 -> 9/25)

The full-pass scorecard showed the movement-agent paradigm covers ~6 games but most failures are games
with a DIFFERENT mechanic. A dispatch-classifier was prototyped and rejected: paradigms do NOT cleanly
separate at the pixel representation (a simple change-type classifier labels almost everything 'growth',
and even cn04 -- which solves via translate -- mislabels). The realistic architecture is TRY-PARADIGMS
ESCALATION, not classify-then-dispatch.

Added a third escalation tier: the CLICK-INTERACTION paradigm (click_config_explore) for pure-click
games with NO moving agent (su15 click-to-connect, lp85 click-only, r11l click-to-template). BFS clicking
object centroids with a full-grid-CONFIGURATION state key (the game state IS the configuration, not an
agent position). KEY SIMPLIFICATION: for these games a stumbled level-up directly yields the solution
(the action path is deterministic), so NO goal heuristic is needed -- stumble == solve.

RESULT (spot-check, fully first-contact): su15@7, lp85@5, r11l@3 now SOLVE (all were FAIL_EXPLORATION
before); sp80@4 still solves via the translate tier (NO regression -- the click tier only runs after the
keyboard agent + pieces passes fail). Takes the solver from 6/25 to 9/25. The click tier reuses the same
real-env-confirmed win signal; full 25-game pass re-running to confirm the new total + updated backlog.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
